    "answer": {
      "short": "The points are collinear: $m_{AB}=m_{BC}=-3$, and all three points satisfy $y=-3x+4$.",
      "worked": "Method 1: compare gradients.\n$$\\begin{align*}m_{AB}&=\\frac{1-10}{1-(-2)}\\\\m_{AB}&=-3\\\\m_{BC}&=\\frac{-5-1}{3-1}\\\\m_{BC}&=-3\\end{align*}$$\nThe intervals $AB$ and $BC$ have equal gradients and share $B$, so the three points lie on the same line.\n\nMethod 2: find the line through $A$ and $B$ and test $C$.\n$$\\begin{align*}y-1&=-3(x-1)\\\\y&=-3x+4\\end{align*}$$\nAt $x=3$:\n$$\\begin{align*}y&=-3(3)+4\\\\y&=-5\\end{align*}$$\nThus $C(3,-5)$ lies on the line through $A$ and $B$, so the three points are collinear.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
